 ## Subtopics
 
-### RotateY
-RotateY is a geometric transformation primitive that rotates a point or shape around the Y-axis in 3D space [S1, unofficial]. It serves as a fundamental building block for constructing camera poses and deforming Signed Distance Fields (SDFs) [G]. Unlike [Rotation Transformation](2279-rotation-transformation.md), which may imply a general rotation matrix, RotateY specifically isolates the Y-axis component [G]. Unlike [Twist](1722-twist.md), it applies a uniform rotation angle to the entire object rather than a spatially varying one [G]. It is a sibling to [RotateX](2278-rotatex.md) and [RotateZ](2280-rotatez.md) [S1, unofficial].
+### [RotateY](1720-rotatey.md)
+RotateY is a geometric transformation primitive that rotates a point or shape around the Y-axis in 3D space. It serves as a fundamental building block for constructing camera poses and deforming Signed Distance Fields (SDFs) [G]. Unlike [Rotation Transformation](2279-rotation-transformation.md), which may imply a general rotation matrix, RotateY specifically isolates the Y-axis component [G]. Unlike [Twist](1722-twist.md), it applies a uniform rotation angle to the entire object rather than a spatially varying one [G]. It is a sibling to [RotateX](2278-rotatex.md) and [RotateZ](2280-rotatez.md). Choose it when a fixed Y-axis orientation is required for camera alignment or SDF deformation. [RotateY](1720-rotatey.md)
 
 ### [Rotation Matrix Computation](2280-rotation-matrix-computation.md)
